      "writtenOn": "2022-06-23T09:58:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does it make sense to hoist this into the #if above? Otherwise `ec_signal` is dead when this option is disabled.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 160,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 160,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "e99a5d17d8a118ead5658d1d6e3f716f788612b2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ef04eab9_261813bd",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/espi.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 160,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000407
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-23T19:18:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "+1\n\nI think `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWERSEQ` implies `!defined(CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ)` as we won\u0027t enable 2 duplicated power sequence code. It is more clear to combine these 2 conditions, i.e. use `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWERSEQ` to replace all `!defined(CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ)` as `CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWERSEQ` is a subset.",
      "parentUuid": "381b18f0_e93f9081",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 160,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 160,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "e99a5d17d8a118ead5658d1d6e3f716f788612b2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "946f9613_a34a959c",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/espi.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 160,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-23T22:11:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately these conditionals are a bit of a mess. There are tests that reference the VW routines without either CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWERSEQ or CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ defined, and so a conditional of !defined(CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ) is not quite the same as defined(CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_POWERSEQ).\n\nHoisting the IF_ENABLED to the #if also means (for the tests) that zephyr_vwire_to_signal() is no longer used, and I had to add more\nconditional guards to tweak this.",
      "parentUuid": "ef04eab9_261813bd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 160,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 160,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "e99a5d17d8a118ead5658d1d6e3f716f788612b2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "43cf3fab_9628a154",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/espi.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 165,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-23T04:39:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can this be an `#else` instead? The previous `espi_vwire_handler` was only gated on `!CONFIG_AP_PWRSEQ` and it seems easier to read that way.",
      "revId": "e99a5d17d8a118ead5658d1d6e3f716f788612b2",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8df53bb8_870ff9af",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/src/espi.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 165,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-23T05:06:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Possibly both could be enabled (e.g a system with legacy power sequencing), or none, or either.\nPotentially I could have used a separate callback for that particular signal, but that would have invoked both callbacks for each VW signal change, which seemed excessive.\nThe change is to essentially treat the PLTRST VW signal specially (when that CONFIG is enabled), regardless which kind of power sequence we are doing.",
      "parentUuid": "43cf3fab_9628a154",
      "revId": "e99a5d17d8a118ead5658d1d6e3f716f788612b2",
